  "Number": 12,
  "Question": "For how many integers \\(x\\) is the point \\((x, -x)\\) inside or on the circle of radius \\(10\\) centered at \\((5, 5)?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\( 11 \\)",
    "B": "\\( 12 \\)",
    "C": "\\( 13 \\)",
    "D": "\\( 14 \\)",
    "E": "\\( 15 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "A point is inside or on the circle exactly when its distance from the center is at most \\(10\\). For \\((x,-x)\\), the horizontal and vertical differences from \\((5,5)\\) are \\(x-5\\) and \\(-x-5\\). The distance formula therefore gives the equivalent condition\n\\[\n(x-5)^2+(-x-5)^2\\le 10^2.\n\\]\nExpanding makes the linear terms cancel:\n\\[\n2x^2+50\\le100,\n\\]\nso \\(x^2\\le25\\), or \\(-5\\le x\\le5\\).\n\nEvery integer in this interval gives a distinct point. Both endpoints satisfy equality in the distance condition, so they are included. The number of integers is\n\\[\n5-(-5)+1=\\boxed{11},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
